//? Title: Gatys style transfer:visible projected Adam through frozen VGG19
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Use genuine pretrained Keras VGG19 weights and original Labrador/Kandinsky images. Explain fixed BGR preprocessing,spatially invariant Gram statistics and exact content/style coefficients. Show all30 projected tensor Adam steps on generated pixels,restore the best image,and prove frozen weights and feature targets remain unchanged. Independent Keras tests verify complete features,objectives and every image derivative.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/gatys_style_transfer.cpp`.

> The method

The learnable object is the generated image,not VGG weights. Frozen source features define content and style objectives;an explicit tensor optimizer updates pixels and projects them into the unit interval. Reproducible official assets,independent gradient fixtures and actual source/output previews connect the mechanism to a measurable short experiment.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/gatys_style_transfer_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/gatys_style_transfer_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/gatys_style_transfer_concept.tikz > build/gatys_style_transfer_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/gatys_style_transfer_concept.svg build/gatys_style_transfer_concept.dvi > build/gatys_style_transfer_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
