\caption(All30 projected Adam updates optimize image pixels through genuine frozen VGG19 features. Raw loss denominators and source targets stay fixed;the best combined objective selects the restored image.)
\alttext(All30 projected Adam updates optimize image pixels through genuine frozen VGG19 features. Raw loss denominators and source targets stay fixed;the best combined objective selects the restored image.)


\image(figures/gatys_style_transfer_change.svg)
\caption(Per-pixel mean absolute change from initialization and restored output mean RGB. The change map is a measured optimization diagnostic,not a saliency claim.)
\alttext(Actual generated-image pixel changes and encoded RGB means.)

\image(figures/gatys_style_transfer_comparison.png)
\caption(Actual content,painting,initial image and restored stylized image,left to right. Every64x64 generated pixel is shown,enlarged four times. This short low-resolution result does not reproduce the paper’s high-resolution convergence.)
\alttext(Genuine Labrador content,Kandinsky style,seeded initialization and the output of30 projected tensor Adam steps.)

The selected final step reduces the combined objective from2.0 to.824895.
Relative content/style losses become.116245/.708650;mean absolute pixel
change is.085392 in encoded unit RGB. The residual image-gradient norm
.051868 confirms this short run has not established a stationary solution.

Feature-loss reduction demonstrates the stated optimization mechanism.
Visual style quality is subjective,and one content/style pair supplies no
held-out generalization score. Average pooling,initial balancing,small image
size and projected Adam are explicit source choices rather than a claim of
exact original-paper rescaling or optimizer reproduction.

> Conclusion

Exact Gram/content checks and independent Keras every-pixel derivatives establish the frozen-feature objective. Thirty visible projected tensor Adam steps then produce a real image-only checkpoint. Unchanged pretrained weights/targets and complete source/result previews keep the short optimization claim concrete.

> References

- [Gatys,Ecker and Bethge,A Neural Algorithm of Artistic Style](https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.06576).
- [Simonyan and Zisserman,Very Deep Convolutional Networks for Large-Scale Image Recognition](https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.1556).
- [Official Keras VGG19 implementation and weight URLs](https://github.com/keras-team/keras/blob/master/keras/src/applications/vgg19.py).
- [TensorFlow style-transfer tutorial,original images and attribution](https://www.tensorflow.org/tutorials/generative/style_transfer).
- [Elf,Yellow Labrador Looking,CC BY-SA3.0](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YellowLabradorLooking_new.jpg).
